r who was otherwise unable to spend fifty dollars on compute, the policy lacks empirical justification. Policymakers should examine who actually pays the cost of these bureaucratic delays and who answers when domestic technical capacity withers under the weight of unworkable oversight. What measurable security gain justifies crushing domestic open-source development when the perimeter is already porous to anyone with a credit card?",
